diff --git a/docs/notes.md b/docs/notes.md
index 7aa1f66..9331a68 100644
--- a/docs/notes.md
+++ b/docs/notes.md
@@ -49,3 +49,34 @@
   non-string texts and wrong shapes are errors. Each question is saved through `Question#option_rows=`, so the
   question-form rules apply (blank options skipped, ≥2 options, ≥1 correct); errors read "Question N: …".
 - Everything runs in one transaction; `QuizTransfer::Invalid` rolls back and the form re-renders (422) with the typed JSON.
+
+## Live game (`Game`, `Player`, `Answer`)
+- `Game(quiz, code, status, question_ids, current_index, version)`. Status: `lobby → open → closed → open … → finished`.
+  "Start" snapshots the ids of the active questions (ordered) into `question_ids` (JSON), so toggling/reordering
+  later doesn't reshuffle a running game. Codes: 5 chars from `Game::CODE_ALPHABET` (no 0/O/1/I), case-insensitive.
+- Transitions (`start!`, `finish_question!`, `advance!`) take the `version` the button was rendered with and do a
+  compare-and-swap `UPDATE … WHERE version = ? AND status = ?`; double clicks / stale tabs are no-ops.
+- `record_answer!` re-reads the game inside the (IMMEDIATE, SQLite) transaction: only the open, current question
+  accepts answers, so nothing slips in after "Finish". One answer per (player, question); re-tapping updates it.
+- `answers.question_id/option_id` have no FKs on purpose (editing a question replaces its options).
+- Routes: `POST /moderate/quizzes/:id/games` ("Start a game"), big screen `GET /moderate/games/:id`
+  (+ `start`, `finish`, `next` (action `advance`), `status` JSON). Players: `/play/:code` (+ `join`, `answer`, `ping`, `leave`).
+- Players: no accounts. Permanent signed cookie `quizzy_browser` (random token) → one `Player` per (game, browser).
+- Players never get correctness data before the question is closed (the open-question view renders no
+  `correct`/`is-correct`; live signals carry no content).
+
+## Live updates (`live_controller.js`)
+- `turbo_stream_from game, :screen` (big screen) / `game, :players` (phones). The server only broadcasts Turbo
+  `refresh` signals (`Game#broadcast_all`, `#broadcast_screen`); pages morph (`turbo_refreshes_with :morph`).
+  Phones only get transitions; the screen also gets joins, first answers, presence changes.
+- Conference Wi-Fi: cable messages can be lost, so `live_controller` also polls (`status` every 2 s on the screen,
+  `ping` every 3 s on phones) and refreshes when the returned version differs from the rendered one; also on
+  `online`/`visibilitychange`/`focus`/bfcache restore. "Reconnecting…" shows after 2 failed polls.
+  Works with WebSockets fully blocked (tested), just with ≤3 s delay.
+- Presence ("Players: N", denominator of "Answers: a / n"): `Player.online` = pinged within `PRESENCE_TIMEOUT` (20 s).
+  `pagehide` sends a `leave` beacon with a per-page-load id; the server ignores a leave from a page that isn't the
+  one that pinged last (so a reload's late beacon doesn't drop the player). Screen version = `"version.online.answered"`.
+- Answer buttons are `button_to` forms (Turbo); `turbo:submit-end` failure shows "Your answer was not sent…".
+- Join input is `data-turbo-permanent` so a refresh doesn't wipe a half-typed name.
+- QR: `rqrcode` gem, inline SVG of the full join URL (`play_url`, same text as shown).
+- Tests: `test/models/game_test.rb`, `test/integration/play_test.rb`, `test/system/game_test.rb` (multi-session).
diff --git a/test/integration/play_test.rb b/test/integration/play_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..217ad13
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/integration/play_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+require "test_helper"
+
+class PlayTest < ActionDispatch::IntegrationTest
+  setup do
+    @game = quizzes(:fest).games.create!
+  end
+
+  test "join, answer without leaking the correct option, results, end" do
+    get "/play/#{@game.code}"
+    assert_response :success
+    assert_select "input[placeholder='Your name']"
+
+    post "/play/#{@game.code}/join", params: { player: { name: "" } }
+    assert_response :unprocessable_entity
+
+    post "/play/#{@game.code}/join", params: { player: { name: "Alice" } }
+    assert_redirected_to "/play/#{@game.code}"
+    follow_redirect!
+    assert_select "h1", "Hi, Alice!"
+
+    post "/play/#{@game.code}/join", params: { player: { name: "Alice again" } }
+    assert_equal 1, @game.players.count, "same browser, same player"
+
+    @game.start!(@game.version)
+    get "/play/#{@game.code}"
+    assert_includes response.body, "Too Many Requests"
+    assert_no_match(/correct/i, response.body.gsub(/play-status|Tap an option/, ""))
+
+    post "/play/#{@game.code}/answer", params: { question_id: questions(:http).id, option_id: Option.find_by!(text: "429").id }
+    follow_redirect!
+    assert_select "form .play-option__mark", "Your answer"
+
+    @game.finish_question!(@game.version)
+    get "/play/#{@game.code}"
+    assert_select ".play-status", "Correct!"
+
+    @game.advance!(@game.version)
+    @game.finish_question!(@game.version)
+    get "/play/#{@game.code}"
+    assert_select ".play-status", "No answer"
+    @game.advance!(@game.version)
+    get "/play/#{@game.code}"
+    assert_includes response.body, "The quiz is over"
+    assert_includes response.body, "1 of 2"
+  end
+
+  test "nobody can join after the end" do
+    @game.update!(status: "finished")
+    get "/play/#{@game.code}"
+    assert_includes response.body, "The quiz is over"
+    assert_select "input[placeholder='Your name']", 0
+    post "/play/#{@game.code}/join", params: { player: { name: "Late" } }
+    assert_equal 0, @game.players.count
+  end
+
+  test "unknown code" do
+    get "/play/NOPE1"
+    assert_response :not_found
+    post "/play/NOPE1/ping"
+    assert_response :not_found
+  end
+
+  test "ping returns the version" do
+    post "/play/#{@game.code}/ping", params: { page: "x" }
+    assert_equal({ "version" => "0" }, response.parsed_body)
+  end
+
+  test "big screen requires the moderator" do
+    get "/moderate/games/#{@game.id}"
+    assert_response :unauthorized
+    get "/moderate/games/#{@game.id}", headers: auth_headers
+    assert_response :success
+    assert_includes response.body, "Players: <strong>0</strong>"
+    assert_includes response.body, "/play/#{@game.code}"
+    post "/moderate/games/#{@game.id}/start", params: { version: 0 }, headers: auth_headers
+    assert @game.reload.open?
+    get "/moderate/games/#{@game.id}/status", headers: auth_headers
+    assert_equal "1.0.0", response.parsed_body["version"]
+  end
+end
diff --git a/test/models/game_test.rb b/test/models/game_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..78bbb55
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/models/game_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+require "test_helper"
+
+class GameTest < ActiveSupport::TestCase
+  setup do
+    @quiz = quizzes(:fest)
+    @game = @quiz.games.create!
+    @alice = @game.players.create!(name: " Alice ", browser_token: "a", last_seen_at: Time.current)
+  end
+
+  test "codes are short, unique and looked up case-insensitively" do
+    assert_match(/\A[A-Z2-9]{5}\z/, @game.code)
+    assert_equal @game, Game.find_by_code!(@game.code.downcase)
+    assert_equal "Alice", @alice.name
+  end
+
+  test "plays the active questions in order and ignores stale versions" do
+    assert_not @game.start!(@game.version + 1)
+    assert @game.start!(@game.version)
+    assert_not @game.start!(@game.version - 1), "double click must be a no-op"
+    assert_equal [ questions(:http).id, questions(:socket).id ], @game.question_ids
+    assert @game.open?
+    assert_equal "Question 1 of 2", "Question #{@game.question_number} of #{@game.total_questions}"
+
+    assert @game.finish_question!(@game.version)
+    stale = @game.version
+    assert @game.advance!(stale)
+    assert_not @game.advance!(stale)
+    assert_equal questions(:socket), @game.current_question
+    assert @game.finish_question!(@game.version)
+    assert @game.last_question?
+    assert @game.advance!(@game.version)
+    assert @game.finished?
+  end
+
+  test "answers can change while open and are refused after closing" do
+    @game.start!(@game.version)
+    q = questions(:http)
+    assert @game.record_answer!(@alice, question_id: q.id, option_id: options(:http_a).id)
+    assert @game.record_answer!(@alice, question_id: q.id, option_id: options(:http_b).id)
+    assert_equal 1, @game.answered_count
+    assert_equal({ options(:http_b).id => 1 }, @game.option_counts)
+    assert_not @game.record_answer!(@alice, question_id: q.id, option_id: options(:socket_a).id), "option of another question"
+    assert_not @game.record_answer!(@alice, question_id: questions(:socket).id, option_id: options(:socket_a).id), "not the current question"
+
+    @game.finish_question!(@game.version)
+    assert_not @game.record_answer!(@alice, question_id: q.id, option_id: options(:http_a).id)
+    assert @alice.answer_for(q.id).correct?
+    assert_equal 1, @alice.score
+  end
+
+  test "presence: pings, leaving, and stale leave beacons" do
+    assert_equal 1, @game.online_count
+    @alice.seen!("page1")
+    @alice.seen!("page2") # reloaded
+    assert_not @alice.left!("page1"), "the old page's beacon must not log out the new page"
+    assert_equal 1, @game.online_count
+    assert @alice.left!("page2")
+    assert_equal 0, @game.online_count
+    assert @alice.seen!("page3"), "coming back online is reported"
+
+    travel Player::PRESENCE_TIMEOUT + 1.second do
+      assert_equal 0, @game.online_count
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "deleting a quiz deletes its games" do
+    @game.start!(@game.version)
+    @game.record_answer!(@alice, question_id: questions(:http).id, option_id: options(:http_a).id)
+    assert_difference -> { Game.count } => -1, -> { Answer.count } => -1, -> { Player.count } => -1 do
+      @quiz.destroy!
+    end
+  end
+end
diff --git a/test/system/game_test.rb b/test/system/game_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a994c38
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/system/game_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,101 @@
+require "application_system_test_case"
+
+class GameTest < ApplicationSystemTestCase
+  setup { Capybara.default_max_wait_time = 8 }
+  teardown { Capybara.default_max_wait_time = 2 }
+
+  def player(name, &block)
+    Capybara.using_session(name, &block)
+  end
+
+  test "a full game with two players, live" do
+    quiz = quizzes(:fest)
+    visit_moderate "/moderate/quizzes/#{quiz.id}"
+    click_on "Start a game"
+    assert_text "Players: 0"
+    game = quiz.games.last
+    assert_current_path "/moderate/games/#{game.id}"
+    link = find("[data-testid=join-link]").text
+    assert_match %r{\Ahttp://[^/]+/play/#{game.code}\z}, link
+    assert_selector ".qr svg"
+    assert_selector "h1", text: "Frontend Fest 2026"
+    path = URI(link).path
+
+    player("alice") do
+      visit path
+      fill_in "Your name", with: "Alice"
+      click_on "Join"
+      assert_text "Hi, Alice!"
+    end
+    assert_text "Players: 1"
+
+    player("bob") do
+      visit path
+      fill_in "Your name", with: "Bob"
+      click_on "Join"
+      assert_text "Hi, Bob!"
+    end
+    assert_text "Players: 2"
+
+    click_on "Start"
+    assert_text "Question 1 of 2" # the inactive question is skipped
+    assert_text "Too Many Requests"
+    assert_text "Answers: 0 / 2"
+
+    player("alice") do
+      assert_text "Too Many Requests"
+      assert_no_text "Correct"
+      refute_includes page.html, "is-correct"
+      click_on "418"
+      within("form", text: "418") { assert_text "Your answer" }
+      click_on "429" # changes the answer
+      within("form", text: "429") { assert_text "Your answer" }
+      within("form", text: "418") { assert_no_text "Your answer" }
+    end
+    assert_text "Answers: 1 / 2"
+
+    player("alice") { visit path; assert_text "Too Many Requests"; within("form", text: "429") { assert_text "Your answer" } }
+    assert_text "Answers: 1 / 2"
+
+    click_on "Finish"
+    within("li", text: "429") { assert_text "Correct"; assert_text "1" }
+    within("li", text: "418") { assert_no_text "Correct"; assert_text "0" }
+    player("alice") { assert_text "Correct!" }
+    player("bob") { assert_text "No answer" }
+
+    click_on "Next"
+    assert_text "Question 2 of 2"
+    player("bob") do
+      assert_text "two-way connection"
+      click_on "SMTP"
+      assert_text "Your answer"
+    end
+    assert_text "Answers: 1 / 2"
+    click_on "Finish"
+    player("bob") { assert_text "Wrong!" }
+    assert_no_button "Next"
+    click_on "End quiz"
+    assert_text "The quiz is over"
+    player("alice") { assert_text "The quiz is over" }
+    player("carol") do
+      visit path
+      assert_text "The quiz is over"
+      assert_no_field "Your name"
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "a player who closes the page leaves the count" do
+    quiz = quizzes(:fest)
+    visit_moderate "/moderate/quizzes/#{quiz.id}"
+    click_on "Start a game"
+    path = URI(find("[data-testid=join-link]").text).path
+    %w[Ann Ben].each do |name|
+      player(name) { visit path; fill_in "Your name", with: name; click_on "Join"; assert_text "Hi, #{name}!" }
+    end
+    assert_text "Players: 2"
+    player("Ben") { visit "about:blank" }
+    assert_text "Players: 1"
+    player("Ben") { visit path; assert_text "Hi, Ben!" }
+    assert_text "Players: 2"
+  end
+end
